# No premature UI wrappers

Do not create shared components whose only job is a thin wrap of existing primitives (e.g. `HeaderIconButton` = `Pressable` + `Icon`).

- Use `Icon` (and `Pressable` when tappable) directly at the call site.
- Extract a shared component only when the same non-trivial behavior appears in 3+ places **and** a single change would need to update all of them.
- Prefer a local helper inside one file over a new `shared/` export.
- Follow YAGNI, KISS, DRY, SOLID: fewer files, boring code, no new abstractions “for consistency.”

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — wrapper for one use case
export function HeaderIconButton({ icon, label, onPress }) {
  return (
    <Pressable accessibilityLabel={label} onPress={onPress}>
      <Icon name={icon} size={22} />
    </Pressable>
  );
}

// ✅ GOOD — compose at the call site
<Pressable accessibilityRole="button" accessibilityLabel="Search" onPress={...} hitSlop={8}>
  <Icon name="search" size={22} color={colors.onSurface} />
</Pressable>
```
